  "method": "PJM close-out L2 phase-0 prediction (ZERO LP): the \u00a72 econ bid HR vs the keeper's.\n\nBuild addendum ``docs/records/pjm/PRECOMMIT-pjm-closeout-l2-incremental-hr-addendum-\nbuild-2026-10-02.md`` \u00a76: from the W0 keeper's committed per-unit layer\n(``results/calibration/w0_pjm_span/hourly/unit_marginal_<Y>.parquet``, P1 offer\n``mc``; read-only) and the L2 artifact\n(``data/raw/_validation-source/pjm_cc_incremental_hr.csv``), compute per year\n\n* ``keeper_econ_hr`` - the keeper's CC_REGULAR econ-row heat rate on the plant's\n  own fuel(+RGGI) basis, ``HR_c * (mc_g - vom) / (mc_c - vom)`` (census 0d's\n  construction: the keeper's committed rung is ``base_HR * 1.0``, so fuel cancels),\n  capacity-weighted over econ rows and all 8760 hours;\n* ``l2_bid_hr`` - the \u00a72 bid on the same basis. With ``vom_g == vom_c`` the bid\n  ``max((mc_c - vom) * HR_incr / HR_c + vom, mc_c)`` reads\n  ``max(HR_incr, HR_c)`` MMBtu/MWh exactly, per plant;\n* ``covered_share`` - CC_REGULAR econ capacity whose plant has a committed row,\n  a committed heat rate and a measured slope for the year (gate S6, >= 80 %);\n* ``delta_mc_covered`` - capacity-weighted mean change of the covered econ rows'\n  P1 ``mc`` (L2 bid minus keeper ``mc``), $/MWh, and the median row's sign (S3).\n\nThe keeper's committed P1 ``mc`` stands in for ``mc_base[c]`` (the committed rung\ncarries no mid-curve markup in the keeper: the minload scope is None) and\n``HR_c`` is the measured CC artifact the keeper's fleet carries\n(``measured_cc_heat_rates``), eGRID fallback where the artifact refuses a row -\nboth as census 0d. Uncovered rows keep the floor form under L2, which needs the\nfleet's base cost and is not predicted here; they are reported at the keeper's\nvalue in ``*_all`` columns only.\n\nWrites ``results/phase0/pjm/_pjmco_l2_phase0_prediction.json``.\nRun: ``python3 scripts/probes/_pjmco_l2_phase0_prediction.py [YEAR ...]``\n",
